<title>USA: USDA Nov 12 world grain highlights.</title>
<headline>USDA Nov 12 world grain highlights.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>World grain crops will total 1,841.31 million tonnes in 1996/97, up from 1,701.83 million in 1995/96, and last month's 1996/97 estimate of 1,830.66 million, the U.S. Agriculture Department said Tuesday.</p>
<p>USDA forecast the world wheat crop at 579.06 million tonnes, coarse grains at 883.60 million, and rice at 378.65 million. Oilseed output was pegged at 257.33 million tonnes, and cotton at 87.02 million bales .</p>
<p>World wheat output fell from last month, largely due to a drop in India's crop. Global coarse grain output rose from last month due to larger crops in the U.S., Argentina and Mexico.  </p>
<p>China soybean and soybean meal imports were increased to 1.0 million tonnes and 1.6 million tonnes, respectively, up from last month's estimates of 900,000 of soybean and 1.4 million tonnes of soybean meal.  </p>
